; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; The second hero, and deliberately the first one's opposite.
;
; The archer wins at distance and loses the moment anything arrives. This one has
; no distance to win at: everything he does happens at arm's length, so the whole
; of playing him is deciding when to walk into a room rather than where to stand
; outside it. Nearly every number below is that one sentence, said in figures.
;
; Which of the two is played is DefaultHero in data/world/world.duke. There is no choosing
; screen yet; this is what makes him playable enough to be balanced.
;
; He is NOT a stronger archer. Twice the health and two thirds of the range is a
; different game, not a better hero — and if he ends up simply better, the two
; numbers to look at are AttackRange and Speed, because those are the ones that
; decide whether a mistake can be walked away from.
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

Hero
  Name = Knight
  DisplayName = Garen
  KindOf = [INFANTRY, SELECTABLE, CAN_ATTACK]
  Geometry = Cylinder
    Radius = 5
    Height = 12
  End
  ; Wider than the archer, which is not decoration: a body's radius is what the
  ; pathfinder steers round and what a monster has to reach past. A man in plate
  ; takes up more doorway.
  ; Shorter sight than the archer's 70, and it costs him something real: the
  ; ground opens up around this number, so he walks into rooms he has seen less
  ; of. He does not need the reach — nothing he owns can hit that far — and an
  ; archer's eyes on a swordsman would be map knowledge he has not earned.
  VisionRange = 52
  Modules = [
    GrowableBody
      ; Nearly twice the archer's 550 once his twenty-two strength is on it -- 980 --
      ; and the first half of why he can stand in a room. The second half is
      ; ArmourPercent below, which is a separate axis: health is how long he
      ; lasts, armour is how much each blow is worth.
      MaxHealth = 716
    End,
    MoveUpdate
      ; Slower than 29, and this is the price of the rest of the page. He cannot
      ; leave a fight he has walked into, so walking in has to be a decision.
      ; Before his agility: 19.5 and ten points at 0.15 are 21.
      Speed = 19.5
      ; 0 = turn on the spot, as the archer does. See the note in his block: a
      ; positive rate is SAGE's vehicle behaviour and makes a man drive in arcs.
      TurnRate = 0
    End,
    WeaponUpdate
      ; Twice the archer's 14 a swing, and slower with it: 34 frames against 24.
      ; Worked out, that is 0.88 a frame against his 0.58 -- about half again as
      ; much damage over time, not the same amount in heavier pieces. The extra is
      ; deliberate and it is what he is paid for standing in range: everything he
      ; hits is hitting him back for the whole of it, which is not true of a single
      ; arrow the archer looses from across the room.
      ;
      ; If he turns out to be simply better, this is the second number to cut --
      ; after Speed, and before AttackRange, which is the one that makes him him.
      ;
      ; ★ Before strength, his primary, which adds its twenty-two: 30 a swing.
      Damage = 8
      ; A sword. The whole of the difference: 11 against the archer's 60, which is
      ; inside every monster's own reach rather than far outside it, so he is being
      ; hit for the whole of the time he is hitting.
      AttackRange = 11
      ; ★ 34 FRAMES BETWEEN BLOWS, as ever: the wait after one (ReloadFrames) and the
      ; swing up to the next (PreAttackFrames). The client starts his slash as he winds up
      ; and the blow lands as the blade comes down -- 9 frames, 0.3s, where his clip's
      ; sword is fastest (HeroClipFitTest measures it). Change the clip, re-measure this.
      ReloadFrames = 25
      PreAttackFrames = 9
      ; He swings as he closes, unlike a drawn bow — a swordsman who had to stop
      ; before every blow would never land one on anything that was backing away.
      AttackOnTheMove = Yes
    End,
    ; His sword lands where he stands, as a monster's blow does, and through the
    ; same hand: which is where the keep's shut gate takes a blow struck through
    ; it, so nothing lands -- see Swing.
    Swing
    End,
    ; No Bow and no EyesOnly: both are the archer's, and both are about a shot that
    ; has to cross a room. EyesOnly would also switch off the engine's own target
    ; acquisition, which is exactly what a creature fighting at arm's length wants
    ; left on -- there is nothing between him and what he is hitting.
    ;
    ; Walks to whatever he is told to attack — see HeroBrain, which both heroes use.
    HeroBrain
    End,
    ; Timers for the statuses he wears, as the archer's -- a stun, so far.
    StatusUpdate
    End,
    ; His book holds the mechanics the game needs of him, no skills of his own: see Skills at the end of this file.
    SkillBook
    End,
    Recovery
    End,
    ; His roll (Space) and his run when Shift is held: see the Dodge skill and the Controls block.
    Dodge
    End,
    Sprint
    End,
    ExperienceModule
      ExperienceValue = 0
      ExperienceRequired = [0, 0, 0]
    End
  ]


; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; The knight.
;
; ★ LANGE, since 2026-10-10: phucpham1076's "Lange - Half-Elf Knight" (CC BY 4.0,
; see CREDITS.md), the owner's choice for the Act 1 hero, made into the game's by
; art/lange/export_lange.py -- his sunglasses taken off, his sword made part of him.
; The KayKit knight he replaces (models/characters/heroes/knight.glb) stays: it is the
; kingdom's soldiers' and the Cursed Hero's.
;
; His rig is his own, so he moves by the Lange set (data/animations/lange.duke),
; whose one library is his own file, not by the Humanoid set: no KayKit clip
; moves a bone of his unless art/lange/retarget.py has put it there. Idle and Walk
; came with him; Attack, Hurt, Death and his casts are borrowed (Quaternius, KayKit).
;
; HE IS LEFT-HANDED. Every clip has the sword in his left hand and the right hand
; free, and the shield slung on his back -- as the model was made. Both are in
; his file, so he carries nothing in Held.
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

  Title = Qalqon va qilich

  ; What he shrugs off before a single level, as a percentage. Here rather than
  ; in his creature block because a hero's armour is REWRITTEN from his level and
  ; what he has found every time either changes, so a figure in the template
  ; would not survive his first level. Counted exactly like a breastplate he
  ; found, which means the file's own floor on damage taken still holds.
  ;
  ; The second half of why he can stand in a room -- MaxHealth is the first. Two
  ; axes on purpose: health is how long he lasts and this is what each blow is
  ; worth, and a monster that hits for 8 is a different problem from one that
  ; hits for 40.
  ArmourPercent = 18

  ; He reaches 11, so he walks until he is all but touching it. The archer stops
  ; at 48 and shoots; a swordsman who did that would stand there swinging at air.
  CloseDistance = 8

  Model = models/characters/heroes/lange.glb
  ; GeometryHeight is 12 in his template above and Lange stands 1.760 tall (metres:
  ; the top of his hair, printed by art/lange/export_lange.py), so 12 / 1.760. He
  ; stands as tall on screen as the KayKit knight did at 4.72; he only looks
  ; slighter, because his head is a man's and not half his height.
  ModelScale = 6.82
  ; His file faces glTF's +Z, as the KayKit people do.
  Facing = 90

  ; His own clips, in his own file -- see data/animations/lange.duke. Named here
  ; as well as there so this block says what he plays. Idle and Walk came with him;
  ; the rest are borrowed from two CC0 libraries and put on his rig by
  ; art/lange/retarget.py.
  Animations = Lange
  Idle = Idle
  ; ★ A RUN, since 2026-10-15. Speed 21 on a man 12 tall is 3.1 m/s for one 1.76 m high:
  ; a jog, not a walk. His own download's walk planted his feet at a quarter of that, and
  ; he skated (the owner: it "doesn't stick"). Walk is now Quaternius' walk and jog half
  ; and half (art/lange/export_lange.py), a long-striding run.
  Walk = Walk
  ; How far one play of it carries him, in units. The client plays it at the rate that
  ; covers this at his speed, so his feet stay where they land however fast he is made to
  ; go. Measured off the clip by HeroClipFitTest: re-export, re-measure.
  WalkStride = 20.6
  ; ★ WIND-UP AND ALL. The client starts this as his weapon winds up, PreAttackFrames
  ; before the blow, so the whole of his slash (Quaternius' Sword_Attack, left-handed) is
  ; seen and the blow lands as the blade comes down. 1.083s, inside the 1.133s between
  ; blows. HeroClipFitTest measures both.
  Attack = Attack
  ; His flinch: played only as he staggers at a heavy blow, for exactly its frames (his STAGGER,
  ; the last of his Skills), when he cannot strike -- so it never covers a swing he really makes.
  Hurt = Hurt
  Death = Death
  ; Struck on the move, a blow (or a flinch) plays from his spine up, his legs running on.
  UpperBody = spine

  ; No Held: his sword and his shield are in his own file -- see the top of this block.
  ; ★ WHAT HE IS MADE OF -- see Attributes in the World block. STRENGTH is his primary: every
  ; point of it is health and swing both, and it grows fastest. At the first level
  ; these make the knight he always was: 716 + 22 x 12 = 980 health,
  ; 19.5 + 10 x 0.15 = 21 speed, 8 + 22 = 30 a swing.
  Primary = STR
  Attributes = [
    Attribute
      Name = STR
      Base = 22
      Growth = 0.8
    End,
    Attribute
      Name = AGI
      Base = 10
      Growth = 0.3
    End,
    Attribute
      Name = INT
      Base = 8
      Growth = 0.3
    End
  ]
  ; ★ WHAT HE CASTS OUT OF, before his intelligence: 10 + 8 x 5 = 50. The shallowest
  ; pool in the game, and his skills are priced to match -- see his Skills.
  ; He is the hero who lives off his ordinary swing, and mana is what stops him
  ; opening with all four and then doing it again.
  MaxMana = 10
  ; Tenths of a point a second: the slowest mana of the three and the quickest
  ; mending. See the note in the Rogue's block.
  ManaRegen = 10
  HealthRegen = 20


; The knight's.
;
; The camera numbers are the same as everybody's, and that is the point: they are
; fractions of whatever they are looking at, so they frame a knight by his own
; measured height without anybody having measured him. If his head comes out badly
; once his model is in, Head and Show are the two lines, and neither needs a
; rebuild.
  ; Standing as he stands in the world, and the pull's raised hand for a level. Fight and
  ; Hurt fall back to standing: a slash looped is a man shadow-boxing, a flinch looped a fit.
  Portrait = PortraitArt
    Calm = Idle
    Dead = Death
    LevelUp = Cast_Pull

    ; ★ NOT the KayKit numbers: Lange is drawn as a man, his head an eighth of him
    ; rather than nearly half, his eyes at about 0.92 of his height. So the camera
    ; looks higher and takes less of him -- head and shoulders.
    Head = 0.88
    Show = 0.36
    Yaw = 22
    Pitch = -4
    Fov = 34
    HurtBelowPercent = 30
    HurtSpeed = 1.5
  End


  ; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  ; He has no skills to buy or cast (the owner, 2026-11-04: the heroes fight with their blows and attack
  ; combinations, skills are the enemies'). What is left in his book is mechanics the game itself needs: his
  ; dodge (Space, the Dodge module), his stagger, his horse (T) and the landing's shockwave (the story casts it).
  ; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Skills = [
    Skill
      ; His dodge, no slot of any bar: pressed on Space (Main.dodge), never bought, his from the start. The Dodge
      ; module of his Modules does it: a roll of Distance toward the way he runs (or faces) over DurationFrames
      ; (0.3s), out of harm's way its first TickFrames (0.23s: no blow takes health or staggers him), through
      ; creatures, short of stone, refused over a seal or while held. Every 2.5 seconds, no mana.
      ; the shoulder drive of his charge, hurried.
      Key = V
      Effect = MODULE
      Distance = 16
      DurationFrames = 9
      TickFrames = 7
      CooldownFrames = 75
      CastAnim = Cast_Charge
      MaxRank = 1
      Name = Chetlanish
    End,
    Skill
      ; His stagger, no slot of the four: never bought, never drawn on his bar, his from the start. A
      ; blow of Damage or more after his armour -- his HeavyBlow's MajorAt in world/feel.duke, what
      ; knocks the screen -- or any critical one stuns him StunFrames (0.37s: his wind-up starts over
      ; after it, his reload waits, no skill casts), his CastAnim (his Hurt) playing for exactly those
      ; frames; and none takes him again for DurationFrames (1.2s) after, so a crowd cannot hold him.
      ; The owner, 2026-10-15: "while the hero flinches he must not attack". Staggered on the move, he
      ; is drawn standing at his flinch and walks on with his order when it ends (E73).
      Key = X
      Effect = STAGGER
      Damage = 45
      StunFrames = 11
      DurationFrames = 36
      CastAnim = Hurt
      MaxRank = 1
    End,
    Skill
      ; His horse, no slot of the four: pressed on T (data/world/mounts.duke), never bought, his from the
      ; start, once he owns a horse (its whistle). Up onto it over WindUpFrames (0.6s), his reach played; a
      ; step or a blow calls it off. Then he rides, BoostPercent quicker, drawn as KnightRiding on the horse's
      ; Saddle bone (E88), his weapon holding fire; off at a second press, a blow (EndsOnHurt), an attack
      ; he orders, a skill (the game gets him off and casts nothing), or a town or an indoor map (NotIn:
      ; the zones the game names, Ichkari for every map that is not out of doors).
      Key = T
      Effect = MOUNT
      ; Up again as soon as he is off: no wait between.
      CooldownFrames = 1
      WindUpFrames = 18
      CastAnim = Gather
      BoostPercent = 100
      Look = KnightRiding
      EndsOnHurt = Yes
      NotIn = [Ichkari, Poytaxt, Olmazor, "Bog'iston", Qoratepa, Tolzor, Yangiobod]
      MaxRank = 1
      Name = Ot
      Icon = icons/items/loot/horse_common.png
    End,
    Skill
      ; The landing's shockwave (docs/plan/2026-10-15-seamless-campaign.md, section 4.3): no key of his, cast by the
      ; story as he comes down in the meteor (CAST PUSH at the landing) -- every enemy within Radius thrown Distance
      ; out over DurationFrames along an arc HitWidth high, stunned StunFrames as it lands (E82). Off his bar, as his
      ; stagger is.
      Key = Y
      Effect = PUSH
      Radius = 160
      Distance = 50
      DurationFrames = 20
      HitWidth = 18
      StunFrames = 90
      Look = Thrown
      MaxRank = 1
      Name = "Qo'nish zarbasi"
    End
  ]
End
